From c15c84e837214aa98300ea8cbe30781d6f06becc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:54:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 53/64] CUDA/HIP: single-token MoE routing (FFN norm, F32
 router, topk_moe) in one launch (GGML_HIP_NORM_ROUTER)

RMS_NORM*MUL of the FFN input (F32 output plus the q8_1 copy for the gate/up MUL_MAT_ID), the F32 router MUL_MAT
and the fused topk_moe nodes run as one kernel (norm_router_topk_f32): one 256-thread block per router row, every
block forms the norm scale itself (the 32 warp sums of rms_norm_mul_f32_unrolled<2>, 4 per warp, same fmas and DPP
order), computes its router row as mul_mat_vec_f<float, float, 1, 256> does, block b writes norm values
32*(b + n_experts*m) + lane (F32 and quantize_q8_1_group), and the block that finishes last (atomic ticket, a new
zeroed per-context counter buffer that each kernel leaves zeroed) runs the topk_moe body (moved into
topk_moe_select, shared with topk_moe_cuda) on all logits. Bitwise as rms_norm*mul + mul_mat_vec_f + topk_moe.
The topk-moe graph matching is moved into ggml_cuda_topk_moe_match_gating (used by both fusions).

GGML_HIP_NORM_ROUTER=0: the three launches.

LFM2.5-24B-A2B Q5_K_M, RX 7900 XTX, KV q8_0: 521 -> 445 kernels/token; the fused kernel 4.9 us vs
2.7 + 2.4 + 3.5 us plus two launch gaps. llama-bench tg128 -r 5, interleaved, 3 rounds:
4.451 -> 4.246 ms/token (off/on, same binary; earlier session 4.505 -> 4.234).

Logit hashes of 64 greedy decode steps (q8_0 and q4_0 KV, depth 0 and 3000) equal to bcdf324d3; greedy md5
LFM plain (q8_0 KV) 2c7ee8a2..., Qwen plain c4708318..., Qwen MTP 6f14e814... unchanged.
test-backend-ops: NORM_ROUTER_TOPK 5/5 (new), TOPK_MOE 416/416.
